<title>FRANCE: Maastricht goals crucial for EMU membership - Delors.</title>
<headline>Maastricht goals crucial for EMU membership - Delors.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former European Commission President Jacques Delors said on Tuesday he wanted Italy to take part in a single European currency but that it and all other EU countries must respect Maastricht-treaty criteria to do so.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody, even the Germans, wants Italy to one day be part of European Economic and Monetary Union, but the criteria are the criteria and we'll see next year which countries can fulfill the conditions,&quot; Delors told RTL radio in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;For those that cannot fulfill them right away, and I mention no names, we can find a transition period with a political solution.&quot;</p>
</text>
